        "research_rationale": "Identity and text: read in full in the registered Federal Register original (7 FR 839-840, issue of 1942-02-10, PDF pages 3-4; grade original_representation_unverified, acceptable_as_original true). The order is headed 'Amending Subdivision VIII of Schedule A of the Civil Service Rules', signed February 6, 1942, bracket [No. 9052]. It amends Subdivision VIII of Schedule A by adding paragraph 30, 'The Solicitor of the Department of the Interior'. Inventory: the amending sentence (which runs across a page break) and item 30; the neighbouring orders on the same pages (EO 9051 and EO 9053) are not part of it. End: EO 9830, signed February 24, 1947, Part III reads \"The following Executive orders are hereby revoked:\" and lists \"No. 9052 of February 6, 1942.\"; the held ACT record locates the provision in the official Federal Register text (12 FR 1259). EO 9830's own Rule II restates Schedule A (section 6.4(a)), and the held text of that restatement contains no entry for the Solicitor of the Department of the Interior.\nMember checks: {\"earlier_end_check\":\"No own-terms end: the order states none. Chain empty. EO 9653 (1945-11-01) amends Schedule A Subdivision VIII paragraphs 12 and 19 only (paragraph headings read), not paragraph 30; no other held order numbered 9053-9829 amends or revokes paragraph 30 (normalised search for 'Subdivision VIII of Schedule A'). An earlier independent AI review of the EO 9830 revocation list (research/excavator/rastell-2026-10-20/r9830/review/REVIEW.jsonl) reached the same finding. Search coverage: the later-events catalogue (OFR disposition notes from 1937) and the held order texts; Public Land Orders and Civil Service Commission notices printed in issues without an executive order are not searched.\",\"independent_command_check\":\"No other command in the order. The later restatement of Schedule A in EO 9830 is a separate command and does not list the position.\",\"savings_check\":\"See savings reason: no savings wording; accrued individual status not established.\",\"scope_check\":\"Both clauses (the amending sentence and paragraph 30) fall under the single revocation of the whole order by number and date; no partial revocation is indicated.\"}",
        "reviews": [],
